    nbf.v4.new_code_cell('print(df.columns.tolist())'),
    nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell('### Data Types'),
    nbf.v4.new_code_cell('df.dtypes'),
    nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell('### Statistical Summary'),
    nbf.v4.new_code_cell('df.describe()'),
    nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell('### Numerical and Categorical Features\n**Numerical Features:** age, trestbps, chol, thalach, oldpeak, ca\n\n**Categorical Features:** sex, cp, fbs, restecg, exang, slope, thal\n\n**Target Variable:** target (0 = No Disease, 1 = Disease)\n\n### Feature Description:\n- **age**: age in years\n- **sex**: sex (1 = male; 0 = female)\n- **cp**: chest pain type (1: typical angina, 2: atypical angina, 3: non-anginal pain, 4: asymptomatic)\n- **trestbps**: resting blood pressure (in mm Hg)\n- **chol**: serum cholestoral in mg/dl\n- **fbs**: fasting blood sugar > 120 mg/dl (1 = true; 0 = false)\n- **restecg**: resting electrocardiographic results\n- **thalach**: maximum heart rate achieved\n- **exang**: exercise induced angina (1 = yes; 0 = no)\n- **oldpeak**: ST depression induced by exercise relative to rest\n- **slope**: the slope of the peak exercise ST segment\n- **ca**: number of major vessels (0-3) colored by flourosopy\n- **thal**: 3 = normal; 6 = fixed defect; 7 = reversable defect\n- **target**: Diagnosis of heart disease (1 = disease present, 0 = disease not present)'),
    nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell('## Phase 2 — Data Cleaning\nWe will check for missing values, duplicates, and outliers.'),
    nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell('### Missing Value Detection'),
    nbf.v4.new_code_cell('df.isnull().sum()'),
    nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell('The UCI dataset originally uses \'?\' for missing values which we converted to NaN during download. We can see missing values in `ca` and `thal`. Since they are few, we will impute them with the median or mode. Why? Dropping them reduces our small dataset, while imputation with mode preserves the distribution for categorical/ordinal data.'),
    nbf.v4.new_code_cell('df[\'ca\'] = df[\'ca\'].fillna(df[\'ca\'].mode()[0])\ndf[\'thal\'] = df[\'thal\'].fillna(df[\'thal\'].mode()[0])\nprint(\'Missing values after treatment:\')\nprint(df.isnull().sum())'),
    nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell('### Duplicate Detection and Removal'),
    nbf.v4.new_code_cell('print(f\'Number of duplicate rows: {df.duplicated().sum()}\')\ndf.drop_duplicates(inplace=True)\nprint(f\'Dataset shape after removing duplicates: {df.shape}\')'),
    nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell('### Invalid Value Detection'),
    nbf.v4.new_code_cell('for col in df.columns:\n    print(f"{col}: {df[col].unique()}")'),
    nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell('All values are within the expected categorical ranges or numerical boundaries.'),
    nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell('### Outlier Analysis\nOutliers in medical data might represent genuine medical conditions (e.g., extremely high cholesterol). We will visualize them but we should be careful before removing them. If cholesterol is 500, it is a high but physiologically possible value (Hypercholesterolemia). Removing such points blindly could reduce model sensitivity to extreme disease cases.'),
    nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell('## Phase 3 — Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\nLet\'s explore relationships between features and the target variable.'),
    nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell('### Target Class Distribution'),
